sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-overall-builder-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029-overall-builder-assessor-claude-fable-5-1> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-029: logarithmic-spiral chamber succession with constant ratio vs Shi (2021) fusulinid half-whorl series (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 77.4/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 2 closes the Pass 1 gaps with measurements rather than assertions. The real fusulinid thin section yields W = 1.49 +/- 0.10 from 13 detected whorl walls, matching Thompson's von Moller value 1.5 and the Dryad Triticites 1.53; Thompson's own Fig. 309 Nummulina yields W = 1.61 +/- 0.18 from 17 wall ratios, a different constant angle (85.7 vs 86.1 deg), which is exactly Thompson's statement that genera differ in the rate of growth. The (W, d, T) sweep shows d alone sets chamber overlap (Globigerina -> Cyclammina), W alone sets coiling tightness, and T sets the helicoid aspect, all monotonically. The verdict machinery now registers the most interesting biology: the early/mid/late drift statistic fails all four pseudoschwagerine genera at 15 % (Triticites 4.6 %), so the pre-registered verdict is MIXED (3/4) — the logarithmic-spiral succession and Thompson's numbers are supported for his exemplar group, but 'near-constant ratio' is not a universal law of foraminiferal shells. Controls behave as designed (shuffled 1/4, arithmetic fails T1, exact-geometric 4/4; the i.i.d. control is a boundary case that passes by construction). Remaining weaknesses: KS rejects normality of residuals (reported, not hidden); the Fig. 309 estimate is coarse; chamber-level (septal) claims remain untested on new specimens; model a0/overlap remain unconstrained by any source value; the environment differs from the lockfile although it is now stamped in the metrics. Overall 77.4/100 (faithfulness 75.1, reproducibility 82.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 12d9d136ee5632ff58f859a3df2645e58ace3576; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, lean 4.35.0, lockfile requirements.lock.txt (NOT the versions used here; the versions actually used are stamped in t1917_029_metrics.json#environment). Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 78, Morphological realism / specimen match 68, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 78, Reproducibility package 78. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py at 12d9d136ee5632ff58f859a3df2645e58ace3576, image/png, 883361 B, 1800×1300 px, artifact_sha256 c266574c8781e151f54da6f411ffab553e81bd8cec52e518212909b9c052d1e3 (sha256 c266574c8781e151f54da6f411ffab553e81bd8cec52e518212909b9c052d1e3), spec_fingerprint a65e5f2d0b7aad60f22deae47babc008c2fa65221e8f2cdd854123ba8884a9f7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a65e5f2d0b7aad60f22deae47babc008c2fa65221e8f2cdd854123ba8884a9f7; artifact_sha256: c266574c8781e151f54da6f411ffab553e81bd8cec52e518212909b9c052d1e3; input_dataset_sha256: {fusulinid_axial_thin_section_commons_NEON.jpg=39f54718bbc8afa2..., shi2020_dryad_sn02v6x26_Landmarks.dat=f7bb3fe73332d58c..., shi2020_dryad_sn02v6x26_Table_1.csv=b5ddc6561b74b26d..., t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_growth.gif=6df0512f746268e7..., thompson1917_fig309_nummulina_antiquior_vonmoller_p591.jpg=e7e37b2c3ea0a6f3...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-029-the-spiral-shells-of-the-foram-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 591-598: chambers/whorls in continued proportion lie on a logarithmic spiral; von Moller's Fusulina whorls in ratio ~1.5 (half-whorl 1.225, alpha ~86 deg); van Iterson's Triloculina 1.323; Rhumbler's Pulvinulina ~1.187 with a 'small secondary fluctuation'; constant volume ratio from growth proportional to existing mass. | Thompson (1917) pp. 601-605: shells differ in constant angle (rate of growth) and in chamber form/overlap; rotaline, Miliolid, Nodosarian, Textularian, Orbitolitid forms are all logarithmic-spiral cases that pass into one another by continuous gradations.; reconstructed_in_script: Discrete similar-chamber generative model (centres r0 rho^k at angle k d, radii a0 rho^k, screw translation T) with a0 = (W-1)/2 and d = 22.5 deg chosen to mimic Fig. 309; chamber overlap and a0 are not source parameters. | Per-specimen log-linear fits of test DIAMETER vs half-whorl stage (PCA frame from the mid-ontogeny outline; longest segment across the 14 two-magnification breaks); BIC vs arithmetic growth; CV and early/mid/late-third drift with Kruskal-Wallis; bootstrap CIs; KS of residuals; Monte-Carlo (normal-null) gap test; thresholds r >= 0.98, 80 %, CV <= 0.15, drift <= 10 %, +/-0.05, p >= 0.05. | CV whorl-wall radii: proloculus pins from the reference JSON (refined +/-6 px for the photograph), sector-median radial profiles, prominence/intensity thresholds 0.06/0.33 (dark walls) and 0.12/0.55 (bright engraving walls); the wall count and the exclusion of the proloculus wall (r < 90 px in Fig. 309) are analyst choices.; transfer_boundary: Dryad outlines are whorl-level axial sections of Late Paleozoic fusulinids in pixels; septal-chamber-level claims (Miliolidae, rotaline forms) are tested only through Thompson's printed tables and the generative model. | n = 1 photograph (640 x 480 px, ~6 whorls per side) and n = 1 engraving (oblique, shaded) for the CV estimates; their W values carry +/-0.10 and +/-0.18 spreads and are consistency checks, not population estimates.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that the growth ratio is physiologically caused by mass-proportional growth (E4 is proved algebraically, not tested). | Does not claim the verdict generalises beyond fusulinids plus one Nummulina engraving; the MIXED verdict is driven by the pseudoschwagerine inflation phase, which Shi (2021) describes as a heterochronic novelty. | Does not claim the KS rejection (p = 7e-4) refutes the law: with 1364 residuals the test detects the S-shaped pseudoschwagerine trajectories and digitisation outliers, i.e. the same deviation that fails T2.." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R10', 'item': 'morphometric-validation: replace the i.i.d. boundary control with a true negative for T2 — a monotone-drift series (ratio rising linearly 1.1 -> 1.4) — so every test has a control that fails it.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R11', 'item': \"specimen-match: give model chambers Thompson's overlap/shape law (p. 602: Globigerina spheres vs Cyclammina overlapped) instead of circles, and fit a0/overlap to the Fig. 309 chamber outlines.\"}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R12', 'item': 'morphometric-validation: test the septal-chamber-level claim on a modern specimen (e.g. a Peneroplis or Elphidium micrograph with visible sutures) so the Miliolid/rotaline part of the claim is measured, not only modelled.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R13', 'item': 'repro-package: run under requirements.lock.txt (or update the lockfile) so the stamped environment and the lockfile agree; version the CV pins (proloculus centres) in the reference JSON with a changelog.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R14', 'item': 'independent second assessor (blinded) before the MIXED verdict is quoted outside this loop.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.774"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 — builder self-audit, Pass 2 (role: builder_assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

